tation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Heun, P., T. Laroche, M.K. Raghuraman, and S.M. Gasser. <year>2001</year>a. The positioning and dynamics of origins of replication in the budding yeast nucleus. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>152</volume>:<fpage>385</fpage>&#x02013;400.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11266454</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Heun, P., T. Laroche, K. Shimada, P. Furrer, and S.M. Gasser. <year>2001</year>b. Chromosome dynamics in the yeast interphase nucleus. <source>Science.</source> <volume>294</volume>:<fpage>2181</fpage>&#x02013;2186.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11739961</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Hochstrasser, M., D. Mathog, Y. Gruenbaum, H. Saumweber, and J.W. Sedat. <year>1986</year>. Spatial organization of chromosomes in the salivary gland nuclei of <italic>Drosophila melanogaster</italic>. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>102</volume>:<fpage>112</fpage>&#x02013;123.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3079766</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Jin, Q., E. Trelles-Sticken, H. Scherthan, and J. Loidl. <year>1998</year>. Yeast nuclei display prominent centromere clustering that is reduced in nondividing cells and in meiotic prophase. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>141</volume>:<fpage>21</fpage>&#x02013;29.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9531545</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Kanoh, J., and F. Ishikawa. <year>2001</year>. spRap1 and spRif1, recruited to telomeres by Taz1, are essential for telomere function in fission yeast. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>11</volume>:<fpage>1624</fpage>&#x02013;1630.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11676925</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Kleckner, N., and B.M. Weiner. <year>1993</year>. Potential advantages of unstable interactions for pairing of chromosomes in meiotic,